Negative control for useContract.meta.ts `isProcessing` (R37 B11).

Spec that must flip: contract.manager-members.int.test.ts
("While my payment-method change is being sent I am told it is in
progress", contract.feature:322) — expects `useMeta().isProcessing` false
before the submit, true while the write is held, false once it lands.

Mutation: reverts the meta flag back to the pre-restore `isSubmitting` name.

diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/useContract.meta.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/useContract.meta.ts
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/useContract.meta.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/useContract.meta.ts
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ export function createContractMeta(
     isLoading: useStateMatches(state, ["subscribing", "loading"]),

     /** True while the payment-method write is being processed, from either parent. */
-    isProcessing: useStateMatches(state, [
+    isSubmitting: useStateMatches(state, [
       "available.changingPaymentMethod.processing",
       "unavailable.changingPaymentMethod.processing"
     ]),
